# Database Rules

## Responsibilities

- Define PostgreSQL schema design principles for legal CRM data
- Enforce multi-tenant isolation, data integrity, and compliance-ready storage
- Standardize indexing, constraints, and query patterns

## Best Practices

- **Multi-tenancy**: Every business entity scoped by `organizationId`
- **Normalization**: 3NF default; denormalize only for proven read performance
- **Immutable financial records**: Invoices/payments never hard-deleted
- **Audit trail**: AuditLog for all create/update/delete on sensitive entities
- **Full-text search**: PostgreSQL `tsvector` for case/client search (Phase 2+)
- **UUIDs/cuids**: External-facing IDs; never sequential integers in URLs
- **Timezone**: Store all timestamps UTC; display in user timezone

## Entity Relationships (Core)

```
Organization ─┬─ User ─── Role ─── Permission
                ├─ Client ─── Case ─┬─ Hearing
                │                   ├─ Document
                │                   ├─ Task
                │                   ├─ Note
                │                   └─ Invoice ─── Payment
                ├─ CalendarEvent
                ├─ Tag
                └─ Setting
Activity / AuditLog / Notification → polymorphic entity references
```

## Coding Standards

- CHECK constraints for valid enum ranges where Prisma enums insufficient
- UNIQUE constraints: `(organizationId, caseNumber)`, `(organizationId, invoiceNumber)`
- NOT NULL on required business fields
- Default values at DB level for status fields
- JSON columns: validate structure in application layer with Zod

## Folder Structure

```
src/prisma/schema.prisma    # Source of truth
src/repositories/           # Query encapsulation
Database.md                 # ERD documentation
```

## Naming Convention

| DB Object | Convention |
|-----------|------------|
| Table | snake_case plural | `cases`, `invoice_line_items` |
| Column | snake_case | `case_number`, `due_date` |
| Index | idx_{table}_{columns} | `idx_cases_org_status` |
| FK | {table}_{column}_fkey | auto-generated OK |

## Performance Rules

- Composite indexes match query WHERE + ORDER BY patterns
- Partial indexes for soft-deleted exclusion: `WHERE deleted_at IS NULL`
- EXPLAIN ANALYZE for queries >100ms in development
- Limit JOIN depth to 3 levels in list queries

## Security Rules

- Application-level RLS backup: always filter `organizationId`
- Consider PostgreSQL RLS policies in production (Phase 3)
- Encrypt PII at rest (cloud provider) — document numbers masked in UI
- Backup retention per legal/compliance requirements (configurable)

## Examples

```sql
-- Index pattern for tenant-scoped lists
CREATE INDEX idx_cases_org_status ON cases (organization_id, status)
  WHERE deleted_at IS NULL;

-- Unique business key per tenant
UNIQUE (organization_id, case_number)
```

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — Always scope by organization
async findCases(orgId: string, filters: CaseFilters) {
  return prisma.case.findMany({
    where: { organizationId: orgId, deletedAt: null, ...filters },
    orderBy: { updatedAt: 'desc' },
    take: 25,
  });
}
```

## Things to Avoid

- Storing calculated totals without reconciliation logic
- Deleting cases with active invoices
- Cross-tenant queries without org filter
- Storing binary files in PostgreSQL
- Missing foreign key constraints

## Checklist Before Finishing Any Task

- [ ] organizationId on all tenant-scoped tables
- [ ] Appropriate indexes for new query patterns
- [ ] Financial records use Restrict, not Cascade delete
- [ ] Soft delete considered for recoverable entities
- [ ] AuditLog entry for sensitive mutations
- [ ] ERD in Database.md updated if schema changed
